            For Markov kernels, this property does not hold: setting
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega=1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times Y
            for every pair of marginals
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %em existence
            part of the universal property: a joint distribution always exists, the product distribution. What fails is the
            %em uniqueness
            part. In other words, the monoidal structure in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stoch"} Stoch
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+limit"} weak product
            but not a categorical
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
          %p
            More generally, given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+monad"} monoidal monad
            on a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+category"} Kleisli category
            is monoidal only when the monad is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functor"} strong monoidal
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markov+category#eqdet"} Markov category
